### Kubernetes (K8s) Architecture ###

                    KUBERNETES CLUSTER
                           |
          ┌────────────────┴────────────────┐
          │                                 │
     CONTROL PLANE                       WORKER NODE
          │                                 │
   ┌──────┼──────────────┐          ┌───────┼─────────┐
   │      │              │          │       │         │
 API   Scheduler    Controller    Kubelet kube-proxy Runtime
Server               Manager        │                 │
   │                               Pod              Container
  etcd                               │
                                     └── Application

>>  control plane :- manage the whole k8's cluster
        
##        1. api-server :- main entry point of kubernetes.

            when you run :- kubectl get pods 
    the req. goes -->> kubectl → API Server → Kubernetes components
          it handles the communication between users components and the cluster.

        2. etcd(Key-value database of Kubernetes)

           It stores cluster information such as:

            Pods
            Nodes
            Deployments
            Services                        ## etcd = Kubernetes database
            Configurations
            Cluster state      

        3. scheduler :- Decides which worker node should run a new Pod.

        New Pod
            ↓
        Scheduler
            ↓
        Worker Node 2
            ↓
         Pod runs

            it considers things such as available resources and scheduling rules.    

        4. controller manager :- Continuously checks whether the actual state matches the desired state.
         example;-
                     you specify :- replicas: 3
                     but only 2 pods are running then,
                    
                     Desired = 3 Pods
                     Actual  = 2 Pods
                        ↓
                    Controller Manager
                        ↓
                    Creates 1 Pod   

****************************************************************************************************************

##      2. Worker Node :- Worker nodes are where your applications actually run
      
         1. kubelet :- The agent running on each worker node.
            It communicates with the API Server and makes sure the Pods/containers assigned to that node are running.

                API Server
                    ↓
                Kubelet
                    ↓
                Pod

         2. container runtime ;- run the container 
              examples :- containerd
                          cri-o                          

                    Kubelet
                    ↓
                    Container Runtime
                    ↓
                    Container

         3. kube-proxy :- help implement kubernetes services networking and forwarding of 
                          traffic to appopriate pods.

                            Client
                            ↓
                            Service
                            ↓
                            kube-proxy / networking
                            ↓
                            Pod

##      3. pod :- A Pod is the smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes.

                        Pod
                        └── Container
                            └── Application                            

                            